WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:02.836 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Well one of the main themes
I have in Only The Strong

00:00:02.836 --> 00:00:05.839 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that the decline sensed
by so many Americans

00:00:05.839 --> 00:00:09.075 align:start size:88% position:13%
is not an accident,
it's declined by design.

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:11.945 align:start size:94% position:6%
The left has had a plot
to sabotage American power

00:00:11.945 --> 00:00:13.680
going back 100 years.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:17.617
You see that in so many
facets of their actions.

00:00:17.617 --> 00:00:20.553
Again, look at what they've
done to weaken the military.

00:00:20.553 --> 00:00:22.722 align:start size:97% position:3%
It's almost like birds
migrating south to the winter.

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:24.858 align:start size:84% position:16%
Every time a Democrat
takes office,

00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:26.626
he cuts the defense budget.

00:00:26.626 --> 00:00:30.130
They've also begun to
distract the military

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:31.331
from its core mission,

00:00:31.331 --> 00:00:34.167
which is preparing
for and winning wars,

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:38.071
using all kinds of critical
race theory, indoctrination,

00:00:38.071 --> 00:00:40.073
or gender ideology obsessions,

00:00:40.073 --> 00:00:43.043 align:start size:84% position:16%
as opposed to focusing
on warfighting.

00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:45.912 align:start size:97% position:3%
Or take a look at what they've
done to energy production

00:00:45.912 --> 00:00:47.580
in America.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.315
Energy is vital to
our way of life.

00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:51.651
It literally powers our economy,

00:00:51.651 --> 00:00:53.386 align:start size:84% position:16%
and we are the world's
energy superpower

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:56.189 align:start size:84% position:16%
when it comes to oil
and gas and coal.

00:00:56.189 --> 00:00:58.491
Yet Joe Biden and the
Democrats have promised

00:00:58.491 --> 00:01:02.796
to eliminate fossil
fuel production in
America, not curb it,

00:01:02.796 --> 00:01:04.497
not make it cleaner,
but to eliminate it.

00:01:04.497 --> 00:01:05.965
At the same time,

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:08.835 align:start size:97% position:3%
they're dedicated to so-called
green or clean technology.

00:01:08.835 --> 00:01:10.236
Who's the world's superpower

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:11.838 align:start size:94% position:6%
when it comes to so-called
green technology?

00:01:11.838 --> 00:01:13.339
China.

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:15.475
I mean, they may march under
the banner of climate change,

00:01:15.475 --> 00:01:16.943
but the Progressive's
banner looks a lot

00:01:16.943 --> 00:01:19.212
like China's five star flag.

00:01:19.212 --> 00:01:20.680
These are not accidents.

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:22.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
These are things that
they have done on purpose.

00:01:22.849 --> 00:01:25.518
(calming music)

00:01:30.223 --> 00:01:31.424
- I'm Dave Rubin,

00:01:31.424 --> 00:01:32.826 align:start size:81% position:19%
and joining me
today is a Senator

00:01:32.826 --> 00:01:34.627 align:start size:81% position:19%
from the great
state of Arkansas,

00:01:34.627 --> 00:01:37.897
as well as author
of the new book,

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:41.901 align:start size:94% position:6%
Only The Strong:
Reserving the Left's Plot

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:44.137
to Sabotage American Power.

00:01:44.137 --> 00:01:45.738
I think you nailed
it with the title.

00:01:45.738 --> 00:01:48.274 align:start size:97% position:3%
Senator Tom Cotton, welcome
to The Rubin Report.

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:49.809
- Hey Dave, thanks
for having me on.

00:01:49.809 --> 00:01:51.077
It's a real pleasure

00:01:51.077 --> 00:01:51.945
and I look forward to
talking to you about

00:01:51.945 --> 00:01:53.513
Only The Strong today.

00:01:53.513 --> 00:01:55.648
- Well, I've wanted to talk
to you for quite some time,

00:01:55.648 --> 00:01:59.385
and basically this
book is a layout

00:01:59.385 --> 00:02:02.489
of an awful lot of the
history of the lunacy

00:02:02.489 --> 00:02:05.859
that I've been fighting
against on this show.

00:02:05.859 --> 00:02:08.795
So first off, what caused
you to write this book?

00:02:08.795 --> 00:02:10.196
I mean, you're a Senator,

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:13.166 align:start size:97% position:3%
you're fighting the
madness in DC all the time.

00:02:13.166 --> 00:02:14.367
What made you say,

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:15.869 align:start size:84% position:16%
hey, I wanna go
back and and look at

00:02:15.869 --> 00:02:18.872 align:start size:97% position:3%
where some of this came from
and and where it's going?

00:02:18.872 --> 00:02:21.908
- Well Dave, it all started
last year in the aftermath

00:02:21.908 --> 00:02:24.110
of the Afghanistan fiasco.

00:02:25.545 --> 00:02:28.314
At first I was astonished
at Joe Biden's bumbling.

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:31.351
Then my team and I spent
a couple weeks in August

00:02:31.351 --> 00:02:32.819
trying to do everything we could

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:36.956
to get Arkansans and other
Americans out of Afghanistan.

00:02:36.956 --> 00:02:38.925
But as we reflected
on it in the days

00:02:38.925 --> 00:02:41.127
after our departure
from Afghanistan,

00:02:41.127 --> 00:02:43.530
I had so many people ask,
how could this happen?

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:47.901
How could we lose to a
medieval band of savages?

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:49.569
But it also went
deeper than that,

00:02:49.569 --> 00:02:52.572
to things they had
seen in recent years.

00:02:52.572 --> 00:02:55.008 align:start size:88% position:13%
Bill and writers
rampaging in our streets

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:57.343 align:start size:84% position:16%
and tearing down
statues of our heroes,

00:02:57.343 --> 00:02:59.779
trying to defund the police,

00:02:59.779 --> 00:03:01.381 align:start size:84% position:16%
and at least
attacking the police

00:03:01.381 --> 00:03:05.084 align:start size:97% position:3%
when they couldn't defund
them as somehow illegitimate.

00:03:05.084 --> 00:03:08.955 align:start size:97% position:3%
Calling America systemically
racist and oppressive,

00:03:08.955 --> 00:03:11.791
which led to a crime wave
all across our country,

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:13.326
America being a laughing stock

00:03:13.326 --> 00:03:16.462 align:start size:97% position:3%
at the hands of our
adversaries around the world.

00:03:16.462 --> 00:03:19.299 align:start size:97% position:3%
And at the bottom of all
those questions I thought was,

00:03:19.299 --> 00:03:20.934
how did it get to this point?

00:03:20.934 --> 00:03:23.169
Why doesn't America win anymore?

00:03:23.169 --> 00:03:26.139
And I wanted to lay
out for my readers

00:03:26.139 --> 00:03:30.910 align:start size:97% position:3%
exactly how the left in
America has for over 100 years

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:33.446 align:start size:84% position:16%
plotted the sabotage
American power.

00:03:33.446 --> 00:03:36.583
Now I'm not claiming that
Liberals and Democrats

00:03:36.583 --> 00:03:40.153
are necessarily unAmerican
or they hate our country,

00:03:40.153 --> 00:03:42.422 align:start size:81% position:19%
although plenty
are and plenty do,

00:03:42.422 --> 00:03:45.391 align:start size:94% position:6%
but at best, they're
ambivalent about America.

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:47.126
They're anguished about our past

00:03:47.126 --> 00:03:48.928
and uncertain about our future.

00:03:48.928 --> 00:03:51.331 align:start size:84% position:16%
And that's why they've
taken the steps

00:03:51.331 --> 00:03:53.733
over the last 100 years
that they have taken

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:55.635
to weaken our military,

00:03:55.635 --> 00:03:57.971
to entangle us in a network

00:03:57.971 --> 00:04:01.975 align:start size:94% position:6%
of globalist international
institutions,

00:04:01.975 --> 00:04:05.979 align:start size:94% position:6%
to bring American
sources of energy offline

00:04:05.979 --> 00:04:08.615 align:start size:88% position:13%
while we make ourself
more dependent on China.

00:04:08.615 --> 00:04:10.984
All these steps are
part of their effort

00:04:10.984 --> 00:04:12.819 align:start size:84% position:16%
to make America just
another country,

00:04:12.819 --> 00:04:15.021 align:start size:88% position:13%
a more normal place
that doesn't view itself

00:04:15.021 --> 00:04:16.789
as exceptional, or special,

00:04:16.789 --> 00:04:19.425
or that has any special
role attributed to it

00:04:19.425 --> 00:04:21.227
by God and by our founders.

00:04:21.227 --> 00:04:24.197 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I wanted to lay out that
case in Only The Strong,

00:04:24.197 --> 00:04:26.099 align:start size:84% position:16%
as well as a roadmap
of the future.

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:30.270
- So before we dive too
much into the specifics

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:31.504
and everything that
you just said there

00:04:31.504 --> 00:04:32.939 align:start size:81% position:19%
is exactly what
the book is about.

00:04:32.939 --> 00:04:34.107
Since you mentioned Afghanistan

00:04:34.107 --> 00:04:35.208
and that was sort of the genesis

00:04:35.208 --> 00:04:36.676
of why you decided to do this,

00:04:36.676 --> 00:04:38.411
can you talk a little
bit of what it was like

00:04:38.411 --> 00:04:41.014
to be a senator the
few days before,

00:04:41.014 --> 00:04:43.316 align:start size:94% position:6%
when the withdrawal's
happening, and then after?

00:04:43.316 --> 00:04:45.852 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like how much
information did you have?

00:04:45.852 --> 00:04:48.855
Did you guys try to push
back on the withdrawal,

00:04:48.855 --> 00:04:50.757
at least how it
was done perhaps,

00:04:50.757 --> 00:04:52.525
and just were you just ignored,

00:04:52.525 --> 00:04:54.861 align:start size:84% position:16%
or were there any
other plans laid out

00:04:54.861 --> 00:04:57.630
that wouldn't have been as
messy as what we all saw?

00:04:58.831 --> 00:05:01.634
- Yes, a lot of us
did try to explain

00:05:01.634 --> 00:05:04.837 align:start size:94% position:6%
that what we saw in August
was likely to happen.

00:05:04.837 --> 00:05:07.607
We didn't necessarily predict
the exact timing or fashion,

00:05:07.607 --> 00:05:10.977
but the reason why Donald Trump

00:05:10.977 --> 00:05:13.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
never withdrew from
Afghanistan in four years,

00:05:13.079 --> 00:05:15.715
despite the fact that
he obviously wanted to

00:05:15.715 --> 00:05:19.452 align:start size:97% position:3%
was 'cause he was worried that
it would lead to a collapse

00:05:19.452 --> 00:05:21.020
of the Afghan government

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:22.989
and a return of the
Taliban to power,

00:05:22.989 --> 00:05:24.824
which would impair
America's interest

00:05:24.824 --> 00:05:27.593 align:start size:84% position:16%
and threaten Americans
here and abroad.

00:05:27.593 --> 00:05:30.630
But Joe Biden came into
office, and he said,

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:32.265
to hell with all that.

00:05:32.265 --> 00:05:35.101
Remember in 2009 as I lay
out in Only The Strong,

00:05:35.101 --> 00:05:39.005 align:start position:0%
he had insisted then on cutting
and running immediately.

00:05:39.005 --> 00:05:42.141 align:start position:0%
And as Barack Obama's own
Secretary of Defense, Bob Gates,

00:05:42.141 --> 00:05:43.910
said he subjected
President Obama

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:46.045 align:start size:84% position:16%
to something like
Chinese water torture

00:05:46.045 --> 00:05:48.147 align:start size:94% position:6%
when everyone else was
trying to get Barack Obama

00:05:48.147 --> 00:05:50.783
off the dime to make a
decision on Afghanistan,

00:05:50.783 --> 00:05:54.187 align:start size:97% position:3%
to commit the troops necessary
to achieve the strategy

00:05:54.187 --> 00:05:57.423 align:start size:94% position:6%
he himself had proclaimed
in the 2008 campaign,

00:05:57.423 --> 00:05:59.692 align:start size:84% position:16%
Joe Biden kept
nattering in his ear,

00:05:59.692 --> 00:06:01.894
seeding mistrust
with our military,

00:06:01.894 --> 00:06:04.197 align:start size:97% position:3%
saying that this mission
could never be accomplished.

00:06:04.197 --> 00:06:06.966
And he carried a chip on
his shoulder for 12 years

00:06:06.966 --> 00:06:08.534 align:start size:84% position:16%
that Barack Obama
didn't listen to him.

00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:11.437
And I think he got
into office in 2021.

00:06:11.437 --> 00:06:16.275
And his toxic combination of
incompetence and insecurity

00:06:16.275 --> 00:06:17.744
led him to want to think,

00:06:17.744 --> 00:06:20.246 align:start size:94% position:6%
want to prove that he
had been right all along,

00:06:20.246 --> 00:06:22.949
that Barack Obama
and the Generals,

00:06:22.949 --> 00:06:24.884 align:start size:94% position:6%
and all of those
Republicans and Democrats

00:06:24.884 --> 00:06:27.353
who had criticized him
for 12 years were wrong.

00:06:27.353 --> 00:06:29.422
So in April, 2021 when he said

00:06:29.422 --> 00:06:30.957
we're gonna rip the bandaid off,

00:06:30.957 --> 00:06:34.494
doesn't matter if the Taliban
has fulfilled the conditions,

00:06:34.494 --> 00:06:36.963 align:start size:81% position:19%
that President
Trump set for them

00:06:36.963 --> 00:06:39.031 align:start size:84% position:16%
in the withdrawal
agreement from 2020,

00:06:39.031 --> 00:06:40.199
we are just gonna get out.

00:06:40.199 --> 00:06:41.868
And most perversely of all,

00:06:41.868 --> 00:06:43.369
said we're gonna
get out by 9/11,

00:06:43.369 --> 00:06:45.772 align:start size:84% position:16%
as if that were
somehow a great way

00:06:45.772 --> 00:06:48.574 align:start size:88% position:13%
to honor the sacrifices
and the losses

00:06:48.574 --> 00:06:51.811
that we suffered on that day
and on everyday since then.

00:06:51.811 --> 00:06:56.516
And as time passed from April
to August, it was clear to me,

00:06:56.516 --> 00:06:58.484
partly based on public reports,

00:06:58.484 --> 00:07:01.187 align:start size:97% position:3%
partly based on the
intelligence we were receiving

00:07:01.187 --> 00:07:05.358 align:start size:97% position:3%
that President Biden had not
taken the steps necessary

00:07:05.358 --> 00:07:09.095
to get all Americans out, to
get their family members out,

00:07:09.095 --> 00:07:10.630
to get out green card holders,

00:07:10.630 --> 00:07:13.399
to get out the loyal Afghans
who had served alongside us,

00:07:13.399 --> 00:07:16.002 align:start size:84% position:16%
and they were trending
towards a disaster.

00:07:16.002 --> 00:07:17.170
And when people asked me,

00:07:17.170 --> 00:07:21.040 align:start size:88% position:13%
how did we see the
scenes from August, 2021

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:23.576 align:start size:88% position:13%
where Afghans were
running onto the tarmac,

00:07:23.576 --> 00:07:26.479 align:start size:84% position:16%
they were jumping
onto aircraft wheels

00:07:26.479 --> 00:07:28.014
trying to fly out
of the country.

00:07:28.014 --> 00:07:32.952
They're handing babies over
the barbed wire topped walls

00:07:33.553 --> 00:07:35.188
of the airfield.

00:07:35.188 --> 00:07:40.193 align:start size:84% position:16%
It's Joe Biden's
rank incompetence
that caused all that.

00:07:40.927 --> 00:07:42.128
We knew this was coming.

00:07:42.128 --> 00:07:43.629 align:start size:81% position:19%
He was warned that
it was coming.

00:07:43.629 --> 00:07:45.031
He was warned by members
of his own administration,

00:07:45.031 --> 00:07:47.300
warned by senior
military officials,

00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:49.202
and he simply did
not listen to them.

00:07:49.202 --> 00:07:52.071 align:start position:0%
In fact, just five weeks
before the fall of Afghanistan,

00:07:52.071 --> 00:07:53.773 align:start size:88% position:13%
he was saying there
was no way we would see

00:07:53.773 --> 00:07:57.243
a scene like we saw
in Saigon in 1975,

00:07:57.243 --> 00:08:00.847 align:start position:0%
had to shamefully take off from
our embassy in helicopters.

00:08:00.847 --> 00:08:02.114
That's exactly what we saw,

00:08:02.114 --> 00:08:04.250
and it was because of
Joe Biden's weakness.

00:08:05.618 --> 00:08:08.221 align:start size:97% position:3%
- What do you think a
clean, effective withdrawal

00:08:08.221 --> 00:08:09.455
would've looked like?

00:08:09.455 --> 00:08:11.023 align:start size:81% position:19%
So for those of
us that, you know,

00:08:11.023 --> 00:08:13.259
it was the longest war
in American history,

00:08:13.259 --> 00:08:14.794
in essence, over 20 years.

00:08:14.794 --> 00:08:16.929
It was unclear to
a lot of people

00:08:16.929 --> 00:08:18.564
why we were there at this point.

00:08:18.564 --> 00:08:20.566
Certainly my more
libertarian side

00:08:20.566 --> 00:08:22.101
thought we shouldn't
have even been there

00:08:22.101 --> 00:08:23.636
in the first place.

00:08:23.636 --> 00:08:25.938
But at some point, if you're
gonna wrap these things up,

00:08:25.938 --> 00:08:27.874
it seems like it always is
gonna be somewhat messy.

00:08:27.874 --> 00:08:30.810
What do you think
a decent withdrawal

00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:32.378
actually would've looked like?

00:08:32.378 --> 00:08:34.514
- Well, Dave, first I wanna
go back to the beginning

00:08:34.514 --> 00:08:36.015
of the Afghan War,

00:08:36.015 --> 00:08:38.751 align:start size:97% position:3%
which was almost universally
supported in the Congress

00:08:38.751 --> 00:08:40.219
by the American people

00:08:40.219 --> 00:08:42.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
since that's the land
from which Osama Bin Laden

00:08:42.288 --> 00:08:43.556
and Al-Qaeda had attacked us,

00:08:43.556 --> 00:08:45.791
having been given safe
harbor, that's Taliban.

00:08:45.791 --> 00:08:48.261 align:start size:97% position:3%
There's no question that we
took a lot of twists and turns

00:08:48.261 --> 00:08:50.096
in Afghanistan,
as we did in Iraq

00:08:50.096 --> 00:08:51.364
that we shouldn't have taken.

00:08:51.364 --> 00:08:53.599
Our main interest in Afghanistan

00:08:53.599 --> 00:08:55.334
was to ensure that
it couldn't be used

00:08:55.334 --> 00:08:58.971 align:start size:84% position:16%
as a training ground
and launching pad
for further attacks.

00:08:58.971 --> 00:09:03.209
Our interest there was not to
try to remake Afghan culture.

00:09:03.209 --> 00:09:05.244
It wasn't to try
to improve literacy

00:09:05.244 --> 00:09:06.712
or bring economic development.

00:09:06.712 --> 00:09:08.948 align:start size:97% position:3%
All those are good things
with Afghan people, certainly,

00:09:08.948 --> 00:09:10.850 align:start size:88% position:13%
but it's not in
America's core interest

00:09:10.850 --> 00:09:12.118
that those things happen.

00:09:12.118 --> 00:09:13.753 align:start size:84% position:16%
So there are many
points along the way

00:09:13.753 --> 00:09:16.055
when we should have
taken stock and said,

00:09:16.055 --> 00:09:18.724
we're no longer serving our
vital national interest here.

00:09:18.724 --> 00:09:22.261
One was in 2009, and
then again in 2011

00:09:22.261 --> 00:09:24.430 align:start size:94% position:6%
when Barack Obama
announced a new strategy,

00:09:24.430 --> 00:09:26.098
but telegraphed that he
wasn't committed to it.

00:09:26.098 --> 00:09:28.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'd been there right
before that announcement.

00:09:28.301 --> 00:09:31.037
I'd heard a lot from Afghans

00:09:31.037 --> 00:09:33.005
about their traditional proverb,

00:09:33.005 --> 00:09:34.840
"You have the watches,
but we have the time".

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:36.876
Unfortunately, that
proved to be right.

00:09:36.876 --> 00:09:39.312 align:start size:84% position:16%
What a final departure
from Afghanistan

00:09:39.312 --> 00:09:41.581 align:start position:0%
could have looked like and
probably should have looked like

00:09:41.581 --> 00:09:43.749
under the circumstances
that President Trump

00:09:43.749 --> 00:09:46.118
and later President
Biden inherited,

00:09:46.118 --> 00:09:47.987
was ensuring that
there was enough

00:09:47.987 --> 00:09:51.357
technical and logistical
support to the Afghan army

00:09:51.357 --> 00:09:53.092
to make sure it didn't collapse.

00:09:53.092 --> 00:09:54.560
As I write in Only The Strong,

00:09:54.560 --> 00:09:57.096
President Biden didn't
just withdraw our troops,

00:09:57.096 --> 00:09:59.632
he withdrew the Western
mechanics and contractors

00:09:59.632 --> 00:10:02.401 align:start size:84% position:16%
that kept the Afghan
Air Force flying.

00:10:02.401 --> 00:10:03.669
These kinds of troops

00:10:03.669 --> 00:10:05.137
or even these kind of
civilian contractors,

00:10:05.137 --> 00:10:06.606 align:start size:84% position:16%
they're not frontline
trigger pullers,

00:10:06.606 --> 00:10:08.107
they're not door kickers,

00:10:08.107 --> 00:10:10.242
they're not going out on
raids against the Taliban.

00:10:10.242 --> 00:10:14.280
But their presence did
give the Afghan army

00:10:14.280 --> 00:10:15.915
a lot of moral support,

00:10:15.915 --> 00:10:18.651
a lot of material support
that would've allowed them

00:10:18.651 --> 00:10:22.121 align:start size:97% position:3%
perhaps to maintain
conditions across the country

00:10:22.121 --> 00:10:23.522
that would've forced the Taliban

00:10:23.522 --> 00:10:26.125
to negotiate some kind
of political outcome

00:10:26.125 --> 00:10:27.860
as opposed to enable the Taliban

00:10:27.860 --> 00:10:29.562
to seize the entire country

00:10:29.562 --> 00:10:32.031 align:start size:84% position:16%
in a span of just a
few weeks last summer.

00:10:32.031 --> 00:10:34.133 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Do you know if Biden
had anyone in his,

00:10:34.133 --> 00:10:36.902 align:start position:0%
I mean, look, he's probably
not gonna listen to Tom Cotton,

00:10:36.902 --> 00:10:38.471
but do you know if he
had anyone in his ear

00:10:38.471 --> 00:10:40.006 align:start size:84% position:16%
in the administration
that was going,

00:10:40.006 --> 00:10:42.975 align:start size:94% position:6%
hey Joe, this thing is not
going to go as planned.

00:10:42.975 --> 00:10:44.477
We're gonna get horrific images,

00:10:44.477 --> 00:10:47.513 align:start size:97% position:3%
they're gonna take all our
weapons, et cetera, et cetera.

00:10:47.513 --> 00:10:49.281 align:start size:81% position:19%
- He did almost
everyone, frankly.

00:10:49.281 --> 00:10:51.884 align:start size:84% position:16%
Certainly his uniform
military leaders,

00:10:51.884 --> 00:10:53.819 align:start size:84% position:16%
but also a lot of
his fellow Democrats,

00:10:53.819 --> 00:10:56.355 align:start size:88% position:13%
the people he appointed
to high positions.

00:10:56.355 --> 00:10:58.658
Look, they wanted to
get out of Afghanistan

00:10:58.658 --> 00:11:01.594
just like Donald Trump, just
like Barack Obama before him.

00:11:01.594 --> 00:11:03.663
But they also knew the
dangerous consequences

00:11:03.663 --> 00:11:06.365
that would follow if we
did what Joe Biden did,

00:11:06.365 --> 00:11:09.602
which is simply pull up
stakes without any plan

00:11:09.602 --> 00:11:12.071
to keep the country and the
government stable there.

00:11:12.071 --> 00:11:13.639
And it's not just Afghanistan.

00:11:13.639 --> 00:11:17.076
You saw within weeks of the
withdrawal from Afghanistan,

00:11:17.076 --> 00:11:19.745 align:start size:88% position:13%
Vladimir Putin beginning
to marshal troops

00:11:19.745 --> 00:11:20.980
on the border of Ukraine.

00:11:20.980 --> 00:11:22.982
There's a dangerous
Afghan effect now,

00:11:22.982 --> 00:11:25.284 align:start size:94% position:6%
just like there was a
dangerous Vietnam syndrome

00:11:25.284 --> 00:11:26.786
after Vietnam

00:11:26.786 --> 00:11:28.854 align:start size:97% position:3%
that will reverberate and
harm our country's interest,

00:11:28.854 --> 00:11:31.424 align:start size:84% position:16%
at least as long as
Joe Biden's president.

00:11:31.424 --> 00:11:34.894 align:start position:0%
- Do you think that Putin
basically that day was thinking,

00:11:34.894 --> 00:11:36.395
all right, this is my move now

00:11:36.395 --> 00:11:39.098
because they'll have no
appetite for stopping me?

00:11:40.099 --> 00:11:41.467
- Oh, there's no question.

00:11:41.467 --> 00:11:44.670
I mean, Joe Biden spent
his first year in office

00:11:44.670 --> 00:11:46.272
appeasing Vladimir Putin,

00:11:46.272 --> 00:11:49.442
enticing him and tempting
him to a trial of strength

00:11:49.442 --> 00:11:51.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
to use Churchill's
famous line that I quote,

00:11:51.744 --> 00:11:53.145
in Only The Strong.

00:11:53.145 --> 00:11:54.680
You know, when he
came into office,

00:11:54.680 --> 00:11:58.284 align:start size:97% position:3%
he granted a extension of
the only arms control treaty

00:11:58.284 --> 00:12:00.786 align:start size:97% position:3%
we have left with Russia, with
no concessions whatsoever,

00:12:00.786 --> 00:12:02.855 align:start size:84% position:16%
something Donald
Trump refused to do.

00:12:02.855 --> 00:12:04.757
That was the first
signal of weakness.

00:12:04.757 --> 00:12:06.792
The second signal of
weakness was to allow

00:12:06.792 --> 00:12:09.228 align:start size:88% position:13%
the Nord Stream gas
pipeline to go forward.

00:12:09.228 --> 00:12:11.964 align:start size:97% position:3%
Again, something that Donald
Trump had refused to do.

00:12:11.964 --> 00:12:14.533 align:start size:97% position:3%
Last April when Vladimir
Putin began to build up troops

00:12:14.533 --> 00:12:16.802
on Ukraine's border
for the first time,

00:12:16.802 --> 00:12:19.905
Joe Biden pleaded to have
a fancy summit in Europe

00:12:19.905 --> 00:12:23.576
to elevate Vladimir Putin's
stature internationally.

00:12:23.576 --> 00:12:26.846
When you combine all those
along with the Afghan effect,

00:12:26.846 --> 00:12:29.949
I think Vladimir Putin saw
the window of opportunity

00:12:29.949 --> 00:12:32.118 align:start size:94% position:6%
to achieve what he is
always wanted to achieve,

00:12:32.118 --> 00:12:33.619
as I explained in
Only The Strong,

00:12:33.619 --> 00:12:36.322 align:start size:84% position:16%
which is to reassemble
a Russian empire,

00:12:36.322 --> 00:12:38.023
which starts in Ukraine.

00:12:38.023 --> 00:12:40.893 align:start size:88% position:13%
I think Joe Biden's
weakness throughout 2021

00:12:40.893 --> 00:12:43.796 align:start size:84% position:16%
tempted Putin to go
for the jugular there,

00:12:43.796 --> 00:12:46.332 align:start size:84% position:16%
and now we, and
especially Ukrainians

00:12:46.332 --> 00:12:49.702 align:start size:97% position:3%
are living with the
consequences of that weakness.

00:12:49.702 --> 00:12:51.670
- You mentioned some
of Biden's motives

00:12:51.670 --> 00:12:53.506 align:start size:84% position:16%
and making up for some
of the Obama stuff,

00:12:53.506 --> 00:12:54.440
that sort of thing.

00:12:55.908 --> 00:12:58.210
How much of what's going on,
generally speaking right now,

00:12:58.210 --> 00:12:59.945
whether we're talking
about this withdrawal,

00:12:59.945 --> 00:13:02.581
or the economy, or
now Russia, Ukraine,

00:13:02.581 --> 00:13:03.516
et cetera, et cetera,

00:13:03.516 --> 00:13:06.652
do you think is intentions,

00:13:06.652 --> 00:13:09.288 align:start size:84% position:16%
like actually
intended to harm us,

00:13:09.288 --> 00:13:10.956
which is partly what you're
talking about in the book,

00:13:10.956 --> 00:13:12.858 align:start size:84% position:16%
versus just complete
mismanagement

00:13:12.858 --> 00:13:14.527
and hiring of the wrong people?

00:13:15.928 --> 00:13:18.430 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Well one of the main themes
I have in Only The Strong

00:13:18.430 --> 00:13:21.767 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that the decline sensed
by so many Americans

00:13:21.767 --> 00:13:25.004 align:start size:88% position:13%
is not an accident,
it's decline by design.

00:13:25.004 --> 00:13:27.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
The left has had a plot
to sabotage American power

00:13:27.873 --> 00:13:29.608
going back 100 years.

00:13:29.608 --> 00:13:33.546
You see that in so many
facets of their actions.

00:13:33.546 --> 00:13:36.482
Again, look at what they've
done to weaken the military.

00:13:36.482 --> 00:13:38.651 align:start position:0%
It's almost like birds
migrating south for the winter.

00:13:38.651 --> 00:13:40.786 align:start size:84% position:16%
Every time a Democrat
takes office,

00:13:40.786 --> 00:13:42.555
he cuts the defense budget.

00:13:42.555 --> 00:13:46.058
They've also begun to
distract the military

00:13:46.058 --> 00:13:47.259
from its core mission,

00:13:47.259 --> 00:13:50.062
which is preparing
for and winning wars,

00:13:50.062 --> 00:13:53.966
using all kinds of critical
race theory, indoctrination,

00:13:53.966 --> 00:13:55.968
or gender ideology obsessions

00:13:55.968 --> 00:13:58.938 align:start size:84% position:16%
as opposed to focusing
on war fighting.

00:13:58.938 --> 00:14:01.740 align:start size:97% position:3%
Or take a look at what they've
done to energy production

00:14:01.740 --> 00:14:03.409
in America.

00:14:03.409 --> 00:14:05.110
Energy is vital to
our way of life.

00:14:05.110 --> 00:14:07.446
It literally powers our economy.

00:14:07.446 --> 00:14:09.215 align:start size:84% position:16%
And we are the world's
energy superpower

00:14:09.215 --> 00:14:11.984 align:start size:84% position:16%
when it comes to oil
and gas and coal.

00:14:11.984 --> 00:14:14.320
Yet Joe Biden and the
Democrats have promised

00:14:14.320 --> 00:14:18.724
to eliminate fossil
fuel production in
America, not curb it,

00:14:18.724 --> 00:14:20.392
not make it cleaner,
but to eliminate it.

00:14:20.392 --> 00:14:22.261
At the same time
they're dedicated

00:14:22.261 --> 00:14:24.763
to so-called green
or clean technology.

00:14:24.763 --> 00:14:26.165
Who's the world's superpower

00:14:26.165 --> 00:14:27.766 align:start size:94% position:6%
when it comes to so-called
green technology?

00:14:27.766 --> 00:14:29.268
China.

00:14:29.268 --> 00:14:31.403 align:start size:97% position:3%
And they may march under the
banner of climate change,

00:14:31.403 --> 00:14:32.872
but the Progressives'
banner looks a lot

00:14:32.872 --> 00:14:35.107
like China's five star flag.

00:14:35.107 --> 00:14:36.575
These are not accidents,

00:14:36.575 --> 00:14:38.844 align:start size:94% position:6%
these are things that
they have done on purpose.

00:14:38.844 --> 00:14:41.146
They want to have
$5 a gallon gas.

00:14:41.146 --> 00:14:44.216
They want a military
that is not capable

00:14:44.216 --> 00:14:47.620 align:start size:97% position:3%
of taking the kind of
assertive, confident action

00:14:47.620 --> 00:14:49.555
that Ronald Reagan,
for instance, took.

00:14:49.555 --> 00:14:53.058 align:start position:0%
They want America to be
enmeshed in a globalist network

00:14:53.058 --> 00:14:56.528 align:start size:97% position:3%
of international organizations
and one-sided treaties.

00:14:56.528 --> 00:14:59.431
That's, again, to get back
to one of the main themes

00:14:59.431 --> 00:15:01.367 align:start size:94% position:6%
of Only The Strong,
they're deeply ambivalent

00:15:01.367 --> 00:15:04.603
about American power
and America itself.

00:15:04.603 --> 00:15:05.838
- So I wanna get into that,

00:15:05.838 --> 00:15:08.641
that 100 year march that
got us to all of this.

00:15:08.641 --> 00:15:11.677
One other thing on
the international
front specifically,

00:15:11.677 --> 00:15:14.246
since we've sort of briefly
discussed Russia and Ukraine,

00:15:14.246 --> 00:15:17.016 align:start size:88% position:13%
I mean, do in effect,
are we at war right now?

00:15:17.016 --> 00:15:18.951
I know there's been
no war declared,

00:15:18.951 --> 00:15:21.153
Congress isn't being
called to discuss it,

00:15:21.153 --> 00:15:24.089
but at some point when you are
endlessly funding something,

00:15:24.089 --> 00:15:27.293
when you are training troops,
when you are sending weapons,

00:15:27.293 --> 00:15:30.195
I mean, what are you and your
colleagues saying about this

00:15:30.195 --> 00:15:31.664
at this point?

00:15:31.664 --> 00:15:34.233 align:start size:97% position:3%
And should we be calling
Congress to talk about this,

00:15:34.233 --> 00:15:37.036
make some sort of declaration
if that's what we're doing?

00:15:37.036 --> 00:15:39.305
And what do you think Biden
would do about all that?

00:15:39.305 --> 00:15:40.839
I mean, the fact that we're
not even discussing that

00:15:40.839 --> 00:15:43.309
seems rather bizarre to me.

00:15:43.309 --> 00:15:45.444
- Well, the United
States is not at war,

00:15:45.444 --> 00:15:47.913
but we are certainly
supporting Ukraine

00:15:47.913 --> 00:15:50.950
and its right to defend
itself and its territory

00:15:50.950 --> 00:15:52.284
and its homes.

00:15:52.284 --> 00:15:54.019
It's regrettable that
we got to this point,

00:15:54.019 --> 00:15:58.057
which we did again because of
Joe Biden's weakness in 2021,

00:15:58.057 --> 00:16:00.559 align:start size:84% position:16%
which tempted Vladimir
Putin to do exactly

00:16:00.559 --> 00:16:01.760
what he's always wanted do,

00:16:01.760 --> 00:16:03.662
frankly, what he
did in 2014 as well

00:16:03.662 --> 00:16:05.931
the first time he
invaded Ukraine.

00:16:05.931 --> 00:16:08.934
I have to note, as I
do sometimes with my
Democratic friends

00:16:08.934 --> 00:16:11.203 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the Senate, which
always sticks in the Craw,

00:16:11.203 --> 00:16:13.472
that Vladimir Putin has a
habit of invading Ukraine

00:16:13.472 --> 00:16:16.342 align:start size:97% position:3%
when Democrats are presidents,
not when a Republican--

00:16:16.342 --> 00:16:17.609
- Somehow there was
a four year blip

00:16:17.609 --> 00:16:19.111
where it didn't happen, huh?

00:16:19.111 --> 00:16:20.279
- Exactly.

00:16:21.447 --> 00:16:23.882
But we are not at war,
nor should we be at war.

00:16:23.882 --> 00:16:26.118 align:start size:84% position:16%
I, for instance, agree
with the decision

00:16:26.118 --> 00:16:28.253
that we're not gonna
commit American troops

00:16:28.253 --> 00:16:29.855
to fight in Ukraine.

00:16:29.855 --> 00:16:32.091 align:start size:84% position:16%
I disagree, as I write
in Only The Strong,

00:16:32.091 --> 00:16:35.127
that Joe Biden should have
announced that in advance.

00:16:35.127 --> 00:16:37.363
It's a bad thing in
a contest of wills

00:16:37.363 --> 00:16:40.566 align:start size:97% position:3%
to keep telling your
adversary what you won't do.

00:16:40.566 --> 00:16:45.571 align:start size:97% position:3%
It screams hesitancy and
timidity and extreme caution.

00:16:46.772 --> 00:16:48.040
By contrast, look
at Ronald Reagan.

00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:50.542
Ronald Reagan, almost
his entire presidency

00:16:50.542 --> 00:16:55.547 align:start size:94% position:6%
supported Afghan guerillas
against Soviet Russia.

00:16:56.682 --> 00:16:58.117 align:start size:88% position:13%
He never considered
putting American troops

00:16:58.117 --> 00:16:59.952
on the ground in Afghanistan,

00:16:59.952 --> 00:17:01.920
but he also didn't
rule it out publicly,

00:17:01.920 --> 00:17:03.922
frankly, didn't say
much at all publicly

00:17:03.922 --> 00:17:07.226 align:start position:0%
about our efforts in
Afghanistan against the Soviets.

00:17:07.226 --> 00:17:10.963
That's because he understood
that you don't want to simplify

00:17:10.963 --> 00:17:12.731
your adversaries' planning.

00:17:12.731 --> 00:17:14.833
You want to keep
them on their toes,

00:17:14.833 --> 00:17:16.168
you wanna make them uncertain

00:17:16.168 --> 00:17:17.736
about what's gonna happen next.

00:17:17.736 --> 00:17:20.072
So while we're not
at war with Ukraine,

00:17:20.072 --> 00:17:22.074
nor, or I'm sorry, in Ukraine,

00:17:22.074 --> 00:17:24.643
we are standing by Ukrainians

00:17:24.643 --> 00:17:28.180 align:start size:94% position:6%
who are simply fighting
for their primordial right

00:17:28.180 --> 00:17:30.682
to defend their homes
and their territory.

00:17:30.682 --> 00:17:32.518 align:start size:88% position:13%
And we have vital
interest at stake there,

00:17:32.518 --> 00:17:34.319
not just in Europe,
but around the world.

00:17:34.319 --> 00:17:37.790 align:start position:0%
For instance, imagine the signal
it would send to Xi Jinping

00:17:37.790 --> 00:17:39.458
and the Chinese Communist

00:17:39.458 --> 00:17:41.794
if Western efforts
in Ukraine falters

00:17:41.794 --> 00:17:44.129
after just eight or nine months,

00:17:44.129 --> 00:17:46.365
I think you could expect
them to go for the jugular

00:17:46.365 --> 00:17:48.133
in Taiwan very soon after it,

00:17:48.133 --> 00:17:49.401
just like Vladimir Putin did

00:17:49.401 --> 00:17:52.304
after he saw Joe Biden's
weakness in Afghanistan

00:17:52.304 --> 00:17:53.539
last summer.

00:17:53.539 --> 00:17:55.140
- I said I was gonna
only ask you one more

00:17:55.140 --> 00:17:56.375
on the international thing,

00:17:56.375 --> 00:17:57.609
but just extending
that real quick,

00:17:57.609 --> 00:18:00.345
I've had Senator Rand
Paul on a few times,

00:18:00.345 --> 00:18:01.713
and you know, one of
his big things is,

00:18:01.713 --> 00:18:03.949
hey, if we're gonna
give them this money,

00:18:03.949 --> 00:18:06.185 align:start size:97% position:3%
which I know he's not thrilled
about in the first place,

00:18:06.185 --> 00:18:09.188
but if we're gonna do it, can
we at least get some receipts?

00:18:09.188 --> 00:18:12.224
And basically, no, there
seems to be no receipts

00:18:12.224 --> 00:18:13.158
to any of this.

00:18:13.158 --> 00:18:14.626
What do we do about that?

00:18:14.626 --> 00:18:16.462 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean, because I
think a lot of people,

00:18:16.462 --> 00:18:19.231
when they see that, and
another 10 billion here,

00:18:19.231 --> 00:18:21.867
meanwhile Florida, you know,
is crushed with this hurricane

00:18:21.867 --> 00:18:23.869
and could use some money,
or whatever it might be,

00:18:23.869 --> 00:18:25.671 align:start size:88% position:13%
or just give the people
back their money,

00:18:25.671 --> 00:18:27.272
I find that that's
one of the things

00:18:27.272 --> 00:18:28.774 align:start size:84% position:16%
that people are
really upset about,

00:18:28.774 --> 00:18:31.176
that we don't even know who
we're giving the money to.

00:18:31.176 --> 00:18:35.180
- Dave, I hear similar views
at home and across the country

00:18:35.180 --> 00:18:36.415
on the campaign trail.

00:18:36.415 --> 00:18:39.318 align:start size:88% position:13%
I do think we can impose
some tighter controls

00:18:39.318 --> 00:18:41.553 align:start size:88% position:13%
on how this aid is being
provided to Ukraine.

00:18:41.553 --> 00:18:44.156 align:start size:84% position:16%
I expect a Republican
Congress will.

00:18:44.156 --> 00:18:47.025
I think we can also demand
that our European partners

00:18:47.025 --> 00:18:49.495
do more to support
Ukraine as well.

00:18:49.495 --> 00:18:52.464
Now much of our aid that you
read about in the newspapers

00:18:52.464 --> 00:18:55.734
is the inkind value of
the military transfers

00:18:55.734 --> 00:18:56.668
that we are making.

00:18:56.668 --> 00:18:58.137
A lot of that money in the end

00:18:58.137 --> 00:19:01.073
gets spent here in the United
States on high paying jobs

00:19:01.073 --> 00:19:02.708
in our defense industry.

00:19:02.708 --> 00:19:04.343
Some of our European partners

00:19:04.343 --> 00:19:06.478
don't have that kind of
mature defense industry.

00:19:06.478 --> 00:19:09.381 align:start size:97% position:3%
They don't have that much
many weapons they can supply.

00:19:09.381 --> 00:19:10.883
They should be stepping forward

00:19:10.883 --> 00:19:13.619
and providing more of the
direct financial support

00:19:13.619 --> 00:19:15.120
to the government in Ukraine,

00:19:15.120 --> 00:19:18.090
so it can not just support its
military on the front lines,

00:19:18.090 --> 00:19:19.925
but its people as well.

00:19:19.925 --> 00:19:22.561
But I do think that we can
have more accountability

00:19:22.561 --> 00:19:23.996 align:start size:84% position:16%
for what has
happened in Ukraine,

00:19:23.996 --> 00:19:26.198
and certainly what will
happen in the future,

00:19:26.198 --> 00:19:28.000
and we can demand a
greater contribution

00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:30.002
from our European allies.

00:19:30.002 --> 00:19:31.303 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Okay, so let's
back up to something

00:19:31.303 --> 00:19:32.638 align:start size:88% position:13%
that you mentioned
about the book earlier.

00:19:32.638 --> 00:19:34.673
You said about 100 year march.

00:19:34.673 --> 00:19:36.108
And you know, a lot of
people when they ask me,

00:19:36.108 --> 00:19:37.376
Dave, when did this crazy

00:19:37.376 --> 00:19:40.179 align:start size:88% position:13%
woke leftist progressive
thing happen?

00:19:40.179 --> 00:19:43.182 align:start size:97% position:3%
You know, people talk about,
okay, maybe in the '60s,

00:19:43.182 --> 00:19:46.251
you know, more communist or
socialist leaning professors

00:19:46.251 --> 00:19:48.187
got into the universities,

00:19:48.187 --> 00:19:49.454
and that's really
where it started.

00:19:49.454 --> 00:19:50.989
But you're really
painting a picture

00:19:50.989 --> 00:19:53.692 align:start size:84% position:16%
that began beyond
that Woodrow Wilson,

00:19:53.692 --> 00:19:56.094
can you get into some of
the beginnings of this?

00:19:57.763 --> 00:19:58.997
- Sure, Dave.

00:19:58.997 --> 00:20:00.499
So in Only The Strong,

00:20:00.499 --> 00:20:03.001
I explained that much of
modern left wing thinking

00:20:03.001 --> 00:20:04.436
goes back to the
progressive era,

00:20:04.436 --> 00:20:06.738
specifically Woodrow Wilson,

00:20:07.940 --> 00:20:09.942
who was a professor
of political science

00:20:09.942 --> 00:20:11.710
before he became president.

00:20:11.710 --> 00:20:15.480 align:start position:0%
You know, for the first 100
years or so of American history,

00:20:15.480 --> 00:20:19.284
both parties consistently
appealed to our founders.

00:20:19.284 --> 00:20:21.019
They claimed that
they were the one

00:20:21.019 --> 00:20:23.188 align:start size:84% position:16%
carrying the true
banner of our founding

00:20:23.188 --> 00:20:25.791 align:start position:0%
of the Declaration of
Independence, our Constitution.

00:20:25.791 --> 00:20:27.593
Woodrow Wilson was
the first politician

00:20:27.593 --> 00:20:30.028 align:start size:84% position:16%
to explicitly
repudiate our founding

00:20:30.028 --> 00:20:33.031 align:start size:94% position:6%
in terms that no
politician today would do.

00:20:33.031 --> 00:20:36.969
I mean, Democrats today
certainly will condemn

00:20:36.969 --> 00:20:38.470
certain aspects of our founding,

00:20:38.470 --> 00:20:42.774 align:start position:0%
but they always claim to be
living up to its truest calling.

00:20:42.774 --> 00:20:43.809
Not Woodrow Wilson.

00:20:43.809 --> 00:20:45.043
You can see in his writings,

00:20:45.043 --> 00:20:46.778 align:start size:84% position:16%
which were prolific
as a professor,

00:20:46.778 --> 00:20:49.815
but he explicitly repudiated
the Declaration of Independence

00:20:49.815 --> 00:20:51.617
and the Constitution.

00:20:51.617 --> 00:20:54.019 align:start size:94% position:6%
He said that the
Declaration was outmoded,

00:20:54.019 --> 00:20:56.488
it was fixed in its own time,

00:20:56.488 --> 00:20:58.924 align:start size:97% position:3%
that we all know that
people aren't created equal.

00:20:58.924 --> 00:21:00.792 align:start size:88% position:13%
He said the Constitution
was too rigid,

00:21:00.792 --> 00:21:02.227
he called it Newtonian,

00:21:02.227 --> 00:21:03.762
that it appealed to
the law of gravity

00:21:03.762 --> 00:21:06.898 align:start position:0%
opposed to Darwinian, appealing
to the law of evolution,

00:21:06.898 --> 00:21:09.534
and that it was time that
we'd be able to evolve

00:21:09.534 --> 00:21:11.937 align:start size:88% position:13%
our system of government
and our way of life.

00:21:11.937 --> 00:21:13.005
You know, that's where the term

00:21:13.005 --> 00:21:15.007
in legal thinking comes from,

00:21:15.007 --> 00:21:17.809 align:start size:84% position:16%
the evolving or
living constitution,

00:21:17.809 --> 00:21:19.444
which really just means
the Constitution is dead

00:21:19.444 --> 00:21:21.580 align:start size:88% position:13%
because the Constitution
is supposed to be

00:21:21.580 --> 00:21:24.983
permanent and fixed based
on our permanent and fixed

00:21:24.983 --> 00:21:26.351
human nature.

00:21:26.351 --> 00:21:27.753 align:start size:97% position:3%
And that's where our
founders base their politics,

00:21:27.753 --> 00:21:30.322 align:start size:97% position:3%
where they base their
foreign policy views as well,

00:21:30.322 --> 00:21:34.626 align:start position:0%
that man is a fallen and sinful
creature, but we can still,

00:21:34.626 --> 00:21:36.928
we can still, in the
right kind of system,

00:21:36.928 --> 00:21:39.064
built on the right kind
of moral principles,

00:21:39.064 --> 00:21:43.235
achieve a degree of freedom
and safety and prosperity

00:21:43.235 --> 00:21:45.203
here for unknown in the world.

00:21:45.203 --> 00:21:49.041
Woodrow Wilson and
the Progressives
rejected all of this.

00:21:49.041 --> 00:21:52.144 align:start size:97% position:3%
This is when you begin to
get the administrative state

00:21:52.144 --> 00:21:53.612
with which we're
so familiar today,

00:21:53.612 --> 00:21:54.746
but it's really an innovation

00:21:54.746 --> 00:21:56.581
only going back about 100 years

00:21:56.581 --> 00:21:58.183 align:start size:84% position:16%
when Woodrow Wilson
was president,

00:21:58.183 --> 00:21:59.451
he started creating agencies

00:21:59.451 --> 00:22:00.919
like the Federal
Trade Commission.

00:22:00.919 --> 00:22:03.689 align:start size:97% position:3%
Now you have this entire
alphabet soup of bureaucrats

00:22:03.689 --> 00:22:05.123
who were unelected,

00:22:05.123 --> 00:22:07.125 align:start size:94% position:6%
yet they presumed to
write regulations for us.

00:22:07.125 --> 00:22:08.327
They presume to enforce them,

00:22:08.327 --> 00:22:10.662 align:start size:84% position:16%
they presume to
adjudicate disputes

00:22:10.662 --> 00:22:12.331
involving those regulations,

00:22:12.331 --> 00:22:14.166 align:start size:84% position:16%
which James Madison
said in the Federalist

00:22:14.166 --> 00:22:15.734 align:start size:84% position:16%
is the very
definition of tyranny

00:22:15.734 --> 00:22:18.770 align:start size:88% position:13%
when you accumulate
legislative, executive,

00:22:18.770 --> 00:22:21.740
and judicial power in
a single set of hands.

00:22:21.740 --> 00:22:24.543
So you don't get to the
extreme left wing views,

00:22:24.543 --> 00:22:26.611
the extreme anti-American views

00:22:26.611 --> 00:22:29.047
that you mentioned
until the 1960s,

00:22:29.047 --> 00:22:32.317 align:start size:88% position:13%
but it's not a very long
step from repudiating

00:22:32.317 --> 00:22:34.853 align:start position:0%
our Declaration of
Independence, our Constitution,

00:22:34.853 --> 00:22:36.488
and our founding principles,

00:22:36.488 --> 00:22:39.091
which happen with Woodrow
Wilson and the Progressives

00:22:39.091 --> 00:22:41.827 align:start size:97% position:3%
to having outright
rejection of America itself

00:22:41.827 --> 00:22:43.795
as I lay out in Only The Strong.

00:22:43.795 --> 00:22:46.298
- Yeah, do you think
his full intention

00:22:46.298 --> 00:22:49.534 align:start size:97% position:3%
with the deep state or
whatever you wanna call it,

00:22:49.534 --> 00:22:51.570
but these bureaucrats
and these departments

00:22:51.570 --> 00:22:54.373
that live on forever, well past
the people who founded them,

00:22:54.373 --> 00:22:56.575
that that really was
in some ways to subvert

00:22:56.575 --> 00:22:58.577 align:start position:0%
the Declaration of Independence
and the Constitution,

00:22:58.577 --> 00:23:00.812 align:start size:88% position:13%
meaning if you could
just staff these people,

00:23:00.812 --> 00:23:03.215 align:start size:94% position:6%
these institutions with
enough of your own people,

00:23:03.215 --> 00:23:04.950
then actually the
founding documents

00:23:04.950 --> 00:23:06.618
wouldn't matter that much?

00:23:06.618 --> 00:23:08.086
- Yeah, there's no
question about that,

00:23:08.086 --> 00:23:10.188 align:start size:97% position:3%
and it's not even my opinion
or your opinion, Dave.

00:23:10.188 --> 00:23:12.858 align:start size:94% position:6%
Woodrow Wilson wrote
about this in his essays,

00:23:12.858 --> 00:23:15.594
in his books, he spoke about
it in some of his speeches.

00:23:15.594 --> 00:23:17.095
He believed that
our Constitution,

00:23:17.095 --> 00:23:20.899 align:start position:0%
with its systems of federalism,
and separated powers,

00:23:20.899 --> 00:23:24.102
and checks and balances was
outmoded for modern times.

00:23:24.102 --> 00:23:25.303
It couldn't move fast enough,

00:23:25.303 --> 00:23:27.005
it couldn't move
with enough detail.

00:23:27.005 --> 00:23:29.608 align:start size:84% position:16%
Instead, he
envisioned a supposed,

00:23:29.608 --> 00:23:34.146 align:start position:0%
a rule by supposed nonpartisan,
neutral scientific experts

00:23:34.146 --> 00:23:37.215
who could carefully,
carefully distinguish

00:23:37.215 --> 00:23:40.519
all the competing interests,
rise above those interests,

00:23:40.519 --> 00:23:43.722
and set the rules
for our society

00:23:43.722 --> 00:23:47.659
according to some abstract
notion of right and justice,

00:23:47.659 --> 00:23:50.429 align:start size:84% position:16%
as opposed to politics
being a system

00:23:50.429 --> 00:23:53.665
that recognizes our
imperfect nature,

00:23:53.665 --> 00:23:56.168
that recognizes that
while man's fallen,

00:23:56.168 --> 00:23:58.770
nature means the government
has to be able to control,

00:23:58.770 --> 00:24:00.372
the government has to
be able, for instance,

00:24:00.372 --> 00:24:03.241 align:start size:84% position:16%
to police crime and
ensures civil justice,

00:24:03.241 --> 00:24:05.143 align:start size:84% position:16%
that those same
people are gonna be

00:24:05.143 --> 00:24:06.645
running the government itself.

00:24:06.645 --> 00:24:09.948
The same people running the
government also are fallen

00:24:09.948 --> 00:24:11.483
and sinful creatures.

00:24:11.483 --> 00:24:13.385
Therefore, the government has
to be able to control itself.

00:24:13.385 --> 00:24:15.253 align:start size:88% position:13%
That's why we have
things like federalism,

00:24:15.253 --> 00:24:17.022
why we have things like
separation of powers,

00:24:17.022 --> 00:24:19.825 align:start size:84% position:16%
why we have things
most importantly, like
regular elections.

00:24:19.825 --> 00:24:22.227 align:start size:97% position:3%
All of these things were
innovations at our founding.

00:24:22.227 --> 00:24:23.595
They may seem usual now,

00:24:23.595 --> 00:24:26.064 align:start size:88% position:13%
but they're innovations
at our founding.

00:24:26.064 --> 00:24:28.133
Woodrow Wilson wanted
to get beyond all that.

00:24:28.133 --> 00:24:30.335
He had this idea that
there was gonna be

00:24:30.335 --> 00:24:35.273 align:start size:97% position:3%
this elite cast of scientific
nonpartisan experts

00:24:35.273 --> 00:24:38.510
who would help set the
rules for our society,

00:24:38.510 --> 00:24:42.247
and you know, maybe back
then you could have seen,

00:24:42.247 --> 00:24:43.982
or you could have thought,
well, this needs to happen.

00:24:43.982 --> 00:24:48.153
But after 100 years
of experience with
these bureaucracies,

00:24:48.153 --> 00:24:49.654
who thinks that's
the case anymore?

00:24:49.654 --> 00:24:53.792
I mean, Tony Fauchi may be
the perfect example to steal

00:24:53.792 --> 00:24:56.495
of Woodrow Wilson's ideal

00:24:56.495 --> 00:24:59.831
of a neutral, nonpartisan
scientific bureaucrat.

00:24:59.831 --> 00:25:02.400
Yet that's anything but
what he has behaved like

00:25:02.400 --> 00:25:03.602
over the last year.

00:25:03.602 --> 00:25:05.136 align:start size:84% position:16%
Or thinking about
Lois Lerner at the IRS

00:25:05.136 --> 00:25:07.072
and the Tea Party controversies.

00:25:07.072 --> 00:25:10.675
Or think about Peter Stroke
and Lisa Page at the FBI

00:25:10.675 --> 00:25:14.279
trying to take down
the Trump presidency.

00:25:14.279 --> 00:25:16.381
Who really has faith
that these bureaucrats,

00:25:16.381 --> 00:25:18.083
without any checks,
without any balances,

00:25:18.083 --> 00:25:19.484
without any oversights,

00:25:19.484 --> 00:25:21.920
are operating for
the public good

00:25:21.920 --> 00:25:24.623
as opposed to their
own narrow interest,

00:25:24.623 --> 00:25:27.893
or the partisan interests
of the Democratic Party.

00:25:27.893 --> 00:25:29.461 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Yeah, it actually
sounds far more

00:25:29.461 --> 00:25:31.796 align:start size:84% position:16%
like a dystopian
Philip K. Dick novel

00:25:31.796 --> 00:25:34.699
than it does something
that a future president

00:25:34.699 --> 00:25:35.934
would eventually write.

00:25:35.934 --> 00:25:38.570
When do you think the
Democrats as a party

00:25:38.570 --> 00:25:40.705
completely tipped
over into that,

00:25:40.705 --> 00:25:42.741
because, you know,
if you think only,

00:25:42.741 --> 00:25:46.011
you know, 40 or 50 years,
50 some odd years ago,

00:25:46.011 --> 00:25:49.614 align:start position:0%
JFK as a Democrat asked not
what the country can do for you,

00:25:49.614 --> 00:25:50.715
ask what you can
do for the country,

00:25:50.715 --> 00:25:52.584
is very reverse of,

00:25:52.584 --> 00:25:55.520
oh, just bow to the
state all the time.

00:25:55.520 --> 00:25:58.123 align:start size:94% position:6%
When do you think they
actually fully tipped into

00:25:58.123 --> 00:26:01.726
what we now see with
the modern Democrats?

00:26:01.726 --> 00:26:03.662 align:start size:88% position:13%
- You see it progressing
steadily from Wilson,

00:26:03.662 --> 00:26:05.363
through FDR, and Truman,

00:26:05.363 --> 00:26:08.099
and then getting to
the '60s, about JFK.

00:26:08.099 --> 00:26:11.469 align:start size:97% position:3%
I write a lot about
Kennedy in Only The Strong.

00:26:11.469 --> 00:26:14.105
No doubt he was capable
of soaring rhetoric,

00:26:14.105 --> 00:26:17.742
but it masked a terrible record.

00:26:17.742 --> 00:26:22.480
JFK very much subscribed to
Woodrow Wilson's conception

00:26:22.480 --> 00:26:26.017
of the administrative state,
and technocratic expertise.

00:26:26.017 --> 00:26:28.253 align:start size:94% position:6%
He had all these so-called
best and brightest

00:26:28.253 --> 00:26:30.055
tinkering with the economy,

00:26:30.055 --> 00:26:32.757
most especially in the
Department of Defense,

00:26:32.757 --> 00:26:36.761 align:start size:97% position:3%
tinkering there, disregarding
the wisdom of the men

00:26:36.761 --> 00:26:39.030
who had helped win World War II.

00:26:39.030 --> 00:26:42.734
And as I write in
Only The Strong,

00:26:42.734 --> 00:26:46.504 align:start size:88% position:13%
you see this most
importantly in Vietnam.

00:26:46.504 --> 00:26:50.742 align:start size:94% position:6%
JFK turned Vietnam into
what was a local conflict,

00:26:50.742 --> 00:26:53.278
in which we had one
side, South Vietnam,

00:26:53.278 --> 00:26:55.847 align:start size:97% position:3%
that was capable of fighting
and defending itself

00:26:55.847 --> 00:26:57.349
with our support.

00:26:57.349 --> 00:27:00.418
But thanks to his weakness,
thanks to his indecision,

00:27:00.418 --> 00:27:01.853
thanks to his belief

00:27:01.853 --> 00:27:05.290 align:start size:97% position:3%
in this kind of enlightened
scientific tinkering,

00:27:05.290 --> 00:27:09.961 align:start size:97% position:3%
he and LBJ turned the Vietnam
War into an American war

00:27:09.961 --> 00:27:14.966 align:start size:97% position:3%
that whose legacy has
distorted the views of America

00:27:16.134 --> 00:27:18.870
and turned so many
left wing Democrats

00:27:18.870 --> 00:27:21.673 align:start size:94% position:6%
openly hostile against our
country then and since.

00:27:21.673 --> 00:27:23.942 align:start size:84% position:16%
- So is there any
Democrat that's left?

00:27:23.942 --> 00:27:26.011 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, when you're
talking to your colleagues

00:27:26.011 --> 00:27:27.212
in the Senate,

00:27:27.212 --> 00:27:29.381 align:start size:88% position:13%
I mean, I was a Democrat
for most of my life,

00:27:29.381 --> 00:27:31.816 align:start size:97% position:3%
most of my, you know, that's
what put me on the map.

00:27:31.816 --> 00:27:33.485
I was a Democrat, I was a lefty,

00:27:33.485 --> 00:27:35.487 align:start size:97% position:3%
and I started, you know, seven
or eight years ago saying,

00:27:35.487 --> 00:27:37.389
hey, something's not right here.

00:27:37.389 --> 00:27:40.558 align:start position:0%
And then I kind of just followed
that path down the road.

00:27:40.558 --> 00:27:42.994
And now when I look at the
modern Democrats, it's like,

00:27:42.994 --> 00:27:45.430 align:start size:84% position:16%
man, there is nobody
left that I think

00:27:45.430 --> 00:27:48.166 align:start size:84% position:16%
would represent
perhaps a government

00:27:48.166 --> 00:27:49.934 align:start size:97% position:3%
that maybe would be a
little bigger than you want,

00:27:49.934 --> 00:27:52.704 align:start size:88% position:13%
but not a completely
totalitarian government.

00:27:52.704 --> 00:27:54.305 align:start size:84% position:16%
There seems like
there's nobody left.

00:27:54.305 --> 00:27:55.840
Are they secretly around?

00:27:55.840 --> 00:27:57.609
I mean, do you privately meet
with these people and they go,

00:27:57.609 --> 00:28:00.512 align:start position:0%
boy, the squad's out of
control, but I'm afraid of them.

00:28:00.512 --> 00:28:02.213 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Yeah, I wish I
could say I did, Dave.

00:28:02.213 --> 00:28:06.117 align:start size:97% position:3%
But no, Democrats are like the
squad members and the House

00:28:06.117 --> 00:28:08.453
are fully in the saddle,

00:28:08.453 --> 00:28:11.956
responding in many cases
to the large activist base

00:28:11.956 --> 00:28:13.124
of the Democratic Party.

00:28:13.124 --> 00:28:14.626 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean, when you
think about Democrats

00:28:14.626 --> 00:28:17.362 align:start size:97% position:3%
who believed in a strong,
competent, powerful America,

00:28:17.362 --> 00:28:19.698
the last one I can really
think of is Joe Lieberman,

00:28:19.698 --> 00:28:21.199
and what happened to him?

00:28:21.199 --> 00:28:25.637
The Democrats voted him out
in their own primary in 2006.

00:28:25.637 --> 00:28:28.406 align:start size:88% position:13%
People before him who
were somewhat anomalous,

00:28:28.406 --> 00:28:30.575
like say Scoop Jackson,

00:28:31.743 --> 00:28:33.144 align:start size:84% position:16%
but for a long time
there just hasn't been

00:28:33.144 --> 00:28:34.479
many strong Democrats.

00:28:34.479 --> 00:28:36.981 align:start size:84% position:16%
Now when it comes time
to go to the polls,

00:28:36.981 --> 00:28:39.551 align:start size:94% position:6%
they sometimes might like
to present themselves

00:28:39.551 --> 00:28:42.153
as strong or caring
about your concerns.

00:28:42.153 --> 00:28:44.389 align:start position:0%
And the same way Democrats
have been making a lot of noise

00:28:44.389 --> 00:28:47.092 align:start size:97% position:3%
over the last couple months,
worried about gas prices,

00:28:47.092 --> 00:28:48.293
but it's all a facade.

00:28:48.293 --> 00:28:49.227 align:start size:84% position:16%
What they're really
worried about

00:28:49.227 --> 00:28:51.429
is their own electoral future,

00:28:51.429 --> 00:28:53.732
not about the future of America.

00:28:53.732 --> 00:28:55.433
- So if we flash forward this,

00:28:55.433 --> 00:28:57.836
I know nobody wants to be
in the prediction game,

00:28:57.836 --> 00:28:59.337
especially a sitting Senator,

00:28:59.337 --> 00:29:01.139 align:start size:97% position:3%
but if we flash forward this
to the midterms that are,

00:29:01.139 --> 00:29:04.642 align:start size:97% position:3%
you know, basically in a week
or 10 days at this point,

00:29:04.642 --> 00:29:08.613
I mean, do you sense this red
wave that everyone senses,

00:29:08.613 --> 00:29:10.215
and what do you think about

00:29:10.215 --> 00:29:12.984 align:start size:94% position:6%
